  "why": "The statement (an E2/little-discs operadic structure on the Hochschild cochain complex) was settled in full between 1999 and 2003; several of those proofs are refereed (McClure-Smith in J. AMS, Berger-Fresse in Math. Proc. Cambridge, Kaufmann in Topology, Hu-Kriz-Voronov in Compositio, Voronov in refereed proceedings), so they are whole/digested before the snapshot. The close call is Farr 2025 and the 2026 thesis: Theorem A does cover associative algebras, but Farr's own abstract says it 'recovers' a solution to an already-solved statement. A new proof of a settled statement does not move the problem. What is new in Farr is the canonical centre construction and the scheme/singular version, and that is a changed question, so I answered variant rather than whole/claimed. Campos-Hermans (prestacks), Wang, Batanin-Davydov, Brav-Rozenblyum, Aguilar Martín-Roitzheim and the Lie-algebroid talk are analogues. The Batanin slides are unread and, per the snippet, only background, so none. Tamarkin's papers are about operad formality, and the record disputes whether they prove Deligne's statement at all, so variant/doubtful. No AI system appears in any event.",
